[QUEST190]
Nombre=First steps
Desc=Are you new here? Bah, that doesn't matter rookie! This place is full of annoying and dangerous creatures, be careful as they can hurt you or even kill you. Eliminate them and I will give you a reward.
DescFinal=Great job, here's your reward!
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=1
PosMap=168
DescAudio=1232
DescFinalAudio=1233

[QUEST191]
Nombre=Mortal poison
Desc=One of these invaders has a deadly poison, try to defeat them and if you come back alive, I will reward you with some antidotes to heal you.
DescFinal=Great job! Wait.. Are you okay? Cure yourself with this antidote.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=3

[QUEST192]
Nombre=Wolf skin
Desc=To continue with our work, you must continue walking around here until you meet a Wolf; Finish him off and bring me his skin!
DescFinal=You are a great Warrior!
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=5

[QUEST193]
Nombre=The Big bad wolf
Desc=Among all these wolves, there is one that is feared by all, the great Wolfang. He is the Leader of the Pack and being able to eliminate him would give us the advantage to control them. Finish him off and bring me his skin, let's show this miserable pack who is the leader.
DescFinal=Wow, you did it! Those wolves will learn not to get into our territory
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=2
PosMap=264
DescAudio=1234
DescFinalAudio=1235

[QUEST198]
Nombre=Dragon Exile
Desc=Where have the little dragons gone? This new race has taken over the area and promises to annihilate anyone who enters the Dragon Dungeon. If you manage to defeat Pyrrak and rip out his heart, I'll give you an incredible reward.
DescFinal=Thank you for your help! Here is your reward
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=20
PosMap=11
DescAudio=1555
DescFinalAudio=1556

[QUEST199]
Nombre=Boat
Desc=If you can get me a good amount of Planks, I can create that object that you want so much to navigate!
DescFinal=Let's sail!
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=25
DescAudio=1161
DescFinalAudio=1162

[QUEST204]
Nombre=Winds of Eldoria
Desc=Great warrior, welcome to the lands of Eldoria! Exotic creatures of incalculable power lurk near this village. I've tried to approach, but a Guardian Spirit is preventing me. If you dare to defeat them and obtain the Wind Rune for me, I will reward you with a great spell.
DescFinal=You're back! Many have fallen by the wayside, unable to help me. I appreciate your bravery. Take this wind rune and use it on your adventure!
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=29
PosMap=123
DescAudio=1171
DescFinalAudio=1172

[QUEST206]
Nombre=Blood for Blood
Desc=I've discovered a way to enhance the Summon Piranha spell, but I need the wild essence drawn directly from their carnivorous counterparts. Travel south of this city and eliminate the piranhas dominating the current. Draw on their essence to fuel the spell... and prove yourself worthy of harnessing their fury.
DescFinal=With this spell, you'll be able to defend yourself from any threat on the high seas!
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25
PosMap=78
DescAudio=1424
DescFinalAudio=1425

[QUEST210]
Nombre=Reduce their forces.
Desc=Listen carefully: I am a spy, not a warrior. My job is to observe, listen, and survive. But you... you are hardened iron, hardened in battle. You must enter the Arkhein Drain. There, enemy guards are gathering to march toward the Har Nareth Refuge, where they are preparing for a confrontation. Your mission: reduce their numbers before they can reinforce that position. The chaos you create down there will slow their movements... and that will give us the advantage. When you have reduced enough guards, return to me.
DescFinal=Impressive. I didn't think you'd manage it so effectively.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25
DescAudio=1443
DescFinalAudio=1444

[QUEST212]
Nombre=Royal Exchange
Desc=Wow... so you made it. I didn't expect you to arrive with the Tome of Wisdom intact. Only a few survive the journey to Arkhein without losing it... or losing themselves.
DescFinal=Kael extends his hand and takes the Tome with restrained reverence.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25
DescAudio=1445
DescFinalAudio=1446

[QUEST214]
Nombre=The meeting with Kael
Desc=Congratulations. The leader of the Royal Navy has placed his trust in you and entrusted you with the Royal Scroll. Take this Tome of Wisdom, an essential relic for the responsibility that lies ahead. Your task is simple in its necessity and perilous in its execution: travel to the enemy city of Arkhein and locate the undercover agent known as "Kael Shadowlive." Deliver the Tome and assist him in incorporating classified information that only he possesses. Be aware: in Arkhein, the guards act without mercy. Attempt to infiltrate using all your strength or call for assistance: if you are discovered, defense will be your only option. Guard the Tome with utmost care: its loss would be irreparable for our cause.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25

[QUEST218]
Nombre=Introduction to Blacksmithing
Desc=As workers, one of our great gifts is Mining. Grab a pickaxe and head to the Iron Mines east of Nix and get me about 100 Ingots, the King has requested that we make more weapons for his troops and this will be enough to create several swords. But be careful, there are some fighters in the mines who will seek to take your resources.
DescFinal=Sweat pays with a good reward, take this.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=13
PosMap=34
DescAudio=1155
DescFinalAudio=1156

[QUEST219]
Nombre=Introduction to Carpentry
Desc=We can always demonstrate our strength against natural forces, but we can also use its resources to create ships, crafts, and even bows. Grab a Lumberjack Axe, head into the forest to get 500 Logs and craft 10 Wooden Spoons. The town cook plans to feed the beggars!
DescFinal=The town will appreciate your cooperation, I will send these resources to the cook immediately.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=14
PosMap=78
DescAudio=1228
DescFinalAudio=1229

[QUEST224]
Nombre=Apprentice Scramer
Desc=Defeat 20 Scramers and speak to the Wise Old Man again to receive your reward.
DescFinal=You have brought peace to my home, this award is for you!
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=5

[QUEST225]
Nombre=Adventurer Scramer
Desc=Defeat 40 Scramers and speak to the Wise Old Man again to receive your reward.
DescFinal=You have brought peace to my home, this award is for you!
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=5

[QUEST226]
Nombre=Master Scramer
Desc=Defeat 80 Scramers and speak to the Wise Old Man again to receive your reward.
DescFinal=You have brought peace to my home, this award is for you!
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=5

[QUEST227]
Nombre=White Poison
Desc=Clear the Island so Astrid can peacefully investigate the Light Mushrooms!
DescFinal=Thanks for your help, maybe these mushrooms will help you too.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=1

[QUEST229]
Nombre=The Superior Bond
Desc=Over time, the druid learns that the bond with creatures can transcend known limits. Those capable of mastering the forces of nature can reach a new level of connection with their pets. To perfect your knowledge, you must prove that you are ready to master more powerful creatures and gain the knowledge necessary to learn a new spell.
DescFinal=You have learned to strengthen your bond with creatures and channel the forces of nature in a superior way. Your former mastery of Summon Tamed Pets is now behind you, and you are capable of using a much more powerful version of the spell, capable of summoning stronger and more resilient pets.
Repetible=0
PosMap=56
RequiredLevel=25

[QUEST230]
Nombre=The Roar of Bruin
Desc=That pelt you brought me... magnificent. But it is not enough to create what I have in mind. There is another Bear, one the hunters call Bruin, the Dark One. His strength is unmatched, and his fur is so thick that frost cracks at the touch. He lives in the Bear Woods, northeast of here. He does not always show himself... but when he roars, even the mountains tremble. If you truly desire a mount worthy of legend, bring me his pelt as a token of my courage. Only with its power can I forge the bond between Beast and Rider.
DescFinal=So you've done it... you've defeated Bruin. I can feel his strength, even through his skin. It's like holding winter's fury contained in a single piece. With this, and the silver hide you gave me earlier, the harness will be complete. But what you've gained goes beyond a mount: you've earned the respect of nature itself.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=1
DescAudio=1157
DescFinalAudio=1158

[QUEST231]
Nombre=The Needle and the Claw
Desc=Listen carefully, traveler. I seek a rare pelt, one not all eyes have been privileged to see. This is the Pelt of the Silver Brown Bear, a rarity among rarities; only a few are born under the light of the winter moon with that metallic sheen in their fur. With one of these pelts, I could create something unique: a harness and saddle so sturdy that not even the blizzards of Nix could break them.
DescFinal=Have you really achieved it? That texture, that shine… unmistakable.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=1
DescAudio=1159
DescFinalAudio=1160

[QUEST232]
Nombre=Lynn's Blood
Desc=If you have the courage to enter the Cave of the Nagas and extract a sample of their Blood, and also bring me a special potion, you will be rewarded with great power.
DescFinal=Great job, with this Flash you'll have incredible power!
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=27
PosMap=517
DescAudio=1422
DescFinalAudio=1423

[QUEST233]
Nombre=Fiery Heart of the Leviathan
Desc=At north of this abandoned city lies the most dangerous creature in the sea. Few sorcerers have the courage to face it, but if you prove otherwise, manage to defeat it and tear out its Heart, I can grant you an upgrade to your Blazing Flare.
DescFinal=Great work, get your reward!
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25
PosMap=171
DescAudio=1426
DescFinalAudio=1427

[QUEST248]
Nombre=Poison Potions
Desc=You now have a basic understanding of Alchemy. If you want to acquire the skill of creating Poison Potions, you'll need to complete the following quest.
DescFinal=Great Job! Here you have your recipe, Now you can create strength potions.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=18
DescAudio=1561
DescFinalAudio=1562

[QUEST249]
Nombre=The Fire of the Ancient
Desc=You have come a long way to find me here in Kamal. My name is Vulkano, master of the Ancient Fire. I have aided the greatest sorcerers of this world, but I no longer grant power freely. To prove you are worthy of this knowledge, you must enter the Dragon’s Lair and retrieve 1 Fire Rune. If you succeed, you shall be rewarded.
DescFinal=Few have faced such fury and lived to tell the tale. You are worthy. Watch and learn... this is the ancient spell of the Fire Elementals. From now on, fire answers your call. Use it wisely... or be consumed by it.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=31
PosMap=17
DescAudio=1428
DescFinalAudio=1429

[QUEST250]
Nombre=Antidotote recipe
Desc=You can now create Life and Mana potions, if you want to acquire the ability to create Antidotes, you will have to complete the following mission!
DescFinal=Great job! Here you have your Recipe, now you can create Antidotes.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=10
PosMap=561
DescAudio=1543
DescFinalAudio=1544

[QUEST251]
Nombre=Life potions
Desc=Pay close attention: to acquire the ability to create Life potions, you will have to complete the following mission!
DescFinal=Great job, here is your recipe, now you can create Life Potions.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=6
PosMap=561
DescAudio=1563
DescFinalAudio=1564

[QUEST252]
Nombre=Maná potions
Desc=You can now create Life potions, if you want to acquire the ability to create MANA potions, you will have to complete the following mission!
DescFinal=Great job! Here you have your Recipe, now you can create Mana Potions.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=8
PosMap=561
DescAudio=1565
DescFinalAudio=1566

[QUEST253]
Nombre=Potions of strength
Desc=You Can Now Create Life, Mana, Antidotes, Energy and Agility Potions. If you want to acquire the ability to create strength potions, you will have to complete the following quest!
DescFinal=Great Job! Here you have your recipe, Now you can create strength potions.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=16
PosMap=561
DescAudio=1567
DescFinalAudio=1568

[QUEST254]
Nombre=Agility potions
Desc=You can now create Life, Mana, Antidotes and Energy potions. If you want to acquire the ability to create Agility potions, you will have to complete the following quest!
DescFinal=Great job! Here you have your Recipe, now you can create Agility Potions.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=14
PosMap=561
DescAudio=1569
DescFinalAudio=1570

[QUEST255]
Nombre=Potions of energy
Desc=You can now create potions of Life, Mana and Antidotes. If you want to acquire the ability to create Energy potions, you will have to complete the following quest!
DescFinal=Great job! Here you have your Recipe, now you can create Energy Potions.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=12
PosMap=561
DescAudio=1571
DescFinalAudio=1572

[QUEST256]
Nombre=Level 1 Rider
Desc=Welcome to my Stable. With this series of assignments I've prepared for your entire career, you can become what I once was. To obtain your first Rider level, you must head to the Mines of Doom and extract a Mysterious Fluid from one of the Dactyls. Stay alert; don't underestimate its power.
DescFinal=Great job! Here's this consumable, come back and see me when you're Level 15.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=10
PosMap=188
DescAudio=1358
DescFinalAudio=1359

[QUEST257]
Nombre=Level 2 Rider
Desc=This second quest requires you to approach the entrance to the dreaded Marabel Dungeon. If you manage to clear the entrance, obtain an Orc Axe, and return alive, you will be rewarded.
DescFinal=Great job! Here's this consumable, come back and see me when you're Level 20.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=15
PosMap=188
DescAudio=1360
DescFinalAudio=1361

[QUEST258]
Nombre=Level 3 Rider
Desc=Only adventurers of Level 20 or higher may accept this perilous mission. Within the Dragon Dungeon, an ancient creature lurks in the shadows. The Beholder's gaze can disintegrate the weak and break the minds of the brave. Your objective is clear: remove the Central Eye of the Beholder and bring it back as irrefutable proof of your bravery.
DescFinal=Great job! Here's this consumable, come back and see me when you're Level 25.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=20
PosMap=188
DescAudio=1362
DescFinalAudio=1363

[QUEST259]
Nombre=Level 4 Rider
Desc=The Minions have desecrated the Forsaken Lair, an ancient refuge now corrupted by dark energies. Deep within, they have forged a Daemon Stone, a source of evil power that threatens to unleash chaos beyond its walls. Your mission is clear: enter the Lair, eliminate all the Minions in your path, and retrieve the Daemon Stone before its power spreads. Return with it, and you will be rewarded as a true hero.
DescFinal=Great job! Here's this consumable, come back and see me when you're Level 30.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25
PosMap=188
DescAudio=1364
DescFinalAudio=1365

[QUEST260]
Nombre=Level 5 Rider
Desc=An ice golem has sacked the Village of Eleuria, stealing the sacred Polar Pendant from an Ancient Guardian. The relic keeps the bitter cold at bay. Travel to the Glacier Cave, confront the fearsome creature, and retrieve it. Only those wearing Winter Robes can survive the icy descent and fulfill this ancient duty.
DescFinal=Great job! Here's this consumable, come back and see me when you're Level 35.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=30
PosMap=188
DescAudio=1366
DescFinalAudio=1367

[QUEST261]
Nombre=Level 6 Rider
Desc=The depths of Dungeon Verill have been corrupted by arcane entities. Eliminating 100 Medusae and 50 Witches is required to restore balance. Among the remains may be the Codex Umbrarum Verill, a forbidden manuscript that holds ancient secrets about the creation and curse of the place. Only the worthy may unravel its hidden knowledge.
DescFinal=Great job! Here's this consumable, come back and see me when you're Level 40.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=35
PosMap=188
DescAudio=1368
DescFinalAudio=1369

[QUEST262]
Nombre=Level 7 Rider
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=40

[QUEST263]
Nombre=Level 8 Rider
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=45

[QUEST264]
Nombre=Level 9 Rider
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=47

[QUEST270]
Nombre=The Legacy of Shadows
Desc=The 9 Primordial Stones, scattered across the world and guarded by fearsome guardians, must be reunited to prevent dark forces from unleashing chaos. The last vestige of the sages has fallen into the hands of those who do not understand the power they seek. Now, only you can restore balance or succumb to the abyss.
DescFinal=You have completed the task many have deemed impossible. The 9 Stones are now reunited, and with them, the Chest of the Dark Legacy. Beware, traveler. The power you have unleashed cannot be undone. The fate of the world, at last, rests in your hands.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=35
PosMap=171
DescAudio=1500
DescFinalAudio=1501

[QUEST271]
Nombre=Key Exchange for Armor
Desc=If you have obtained the Darkness Key, claim this quest to obtain your Armor
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=35
DescAudio=1502

[QUEST272]
Nombre=Key Exchange for Robe
Desc=If you have obtained the Darkness Key, claim this quest to obtain your Robe.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=35
DescAudio=1503

[QUEST273]
Nombre=To get the scale.
Desc=With that advantage, the next move has arrived. Deep within the Drainage, where mud mingles with ancient echoes, a creature feared even by its own kind often manifests: the Har Nareth. A colossal beast, half reptile, half something else... something nature would rather forget. Sometimes it appears... sometimes it doesn't. Its presence is capricious, like death itself patiently waiting. If you have the strength, you could try to face it alone. If not... gather allies who aren't afraid to scream among the tunnels. When it falls, take a scale from its body. Just one. It will be more than enough.
DescFinal=Now you must travel to the Isle of Griffins. Among crags and wind, you will find Aduin the Wanderer. He belongs neither to the Crown nor to the Shades; he is a sage who lives observing the world without taking sides. Take this letter to him as soon as possible.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25
DescAudio=1447
DescFinalAudio=1486

[QUEST275]
Nombre=Dagger Poison
Desc=The Abandoned Lair is no longer empty. Corrupted gargoyles cling to its ruins, creatures of stone and poison whose touch infects flesh. A single blow is enough to feel the acid coursing through your veins. From their bodies, Acid Fluid can be extracted, a volatile and extremely dangerous substance. It is the key ingredient in a forbidden art: Toxin Edge. Bring me that fluid, and I will teach you how to poison your daggers like a true assassin. But keep your cool… the gargoyles sense weakness. If fear takes hold, you will not leave the lair.
DescFinal=From now on, your blades will drink poison with every strike. This is the Toxin Edge... Use it wisely, or die by your own hand.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25
PosMap=560
DescAudio=1283
DescFinalAudio=1284

[QUEST279]
Nombre=Learn the recipe for Fire
Desc=Thirga Brumhilda has entrusted you with a burning task. Within the portal to the Forest of Spirits, the Firebearers guard ancient pages of a lost grimoire. Gather 50 Book of Fire Pages, forged in the very heat of creation. Only then will you be able to master the Recipe of the Element of Fire, symbol of the power and passion of the dwarven forge.
DescFinal=Ha! I can smell the smoke on your clothes and see the fire's gleam in your eyes. You have brought the burning blades, and with them, the knowledge of the ancient smiths. From this day forward, fire will answer your hammer. Use this recipe with pride, Worker, and let every blow ignite Morgrim's story!
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25
PosMap=594
DescAudio=1506
DescFinalAudio=1507

[QUEST280]
Nombre=Learn the recipe for Water
Desc=Thirga has spoken to you of the balance of Water, a patient and malleable element. In the Ancestral Vision, the Water Bearers protect the pages of a fluid and ever-changing grimoire. Gather 50 Water Book Pages and prove that you can temper your will like steel beneath the stream. Master the Recipe of the Water Element and let serenity guide your hand.
DescFinal=I see you've learned the lesson of water... patient, constant, unbreakable. Water polishes stone like work polishes a dwarf. Take this recipe and let it flow in your forge. May every drop that falls on the metal remind you who you are.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25
PosMap=594
DescAudio=1508
DescFinalAudio=1509

[QUEST281]
Nombre=Learn the recipe for Wind
Desc=In the Ancestral Vision, Windbearers move amidst invisible gusts, safeguarding volatile power. Thirga Brumhilda challenges you to collect 50 Wind Book Leaves, fragments as light and elusive as a current of air. Only those who understand the freedom of the wind can master the Wind Element Recipe.
DescFinal=You moved swiftly, like a stream through the mountains. The wind is not easily captured, but you have tamed it with your effort. Receive this recipe, and let the breath of the air bless your forges. No wall can contain a free spirit.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25
PosMap=594
DescAudio=1510
DescFinalAudio=1511

[QUEST282]
Nombre=Learn the recipe for Earth
Desc=Thirga's final challenge leads you to the Earth Bearers. Their leaves weigh as much as mountains, and only a truly persevering worker can gather 50 Earth Book Leaves. The Earth Element Recipe represents the stability, strength, and resilience of the people of Morgrim.
DescFinal=Firm as a rock. Thus are true workers forged. You have borne the weight of the earth, and she has accepted you. Take this recipe, son of the forge, and let your craft be as eternal as Morgrim's stone.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25
PosMap=594
DescAudio=1512
DescFinalAudio=1513

[QUEST285]
Nombre=Underground Antennas
Desc=I want you to go into the Anthill. Don't ask too many questions; I don't have the answers yet. The ants are changing... coordinating. I need you to get 60 Ant Antennae. I'll examine their structures, their signals... and I'll know if my suspicions are true. If there's a Queen down there... I don't want Ullathorpe to find out too late. Come back as soon as you have the antennae!
DescFinal=So... my fears were true. These antennae don't belong to ordinary ants. There's a pattern, a frequency... as if something is guiding them. You've done more than you can imagine, traveler. With this information, perhaps we can prepare... before she awakens. Take your reward. And keep this quiet.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=13
PosMap=1
DescAudio=1113
DescFinalAudio=1114

[QUEST286]
Nombre=The Custody of the Frogians
Desc=The frogs of Frogian Cave fiercely protect a rare botanical ingredient: the Shadow Water Lily, a magical plant gland that blooms only in waters magically altered by the presence of arcane amphibious creatures. Its "heart" is a hardened, dark purple seed that beats faintly as if it possessed a life of its own. The ancient inhabitants of Forgat considered this ingredient a natural protector against disease and poison, but over time the Frogian frogs took over the cave and guarded it like a treasure. The presence of sorcerers among them caused the plant to mutate, and today, harvesting it without dying in the attempt has become nearly impossible. If you recover the precious heart, I can continue my herbal research.
DescFinal=By the roots of Milthas! You did it! I thought those creatures would have devoured you, but here you are... and with the Heart of the Shadow Lily in your hands. Look at it... it's still beating. You have no idea how valuable this is to my research. You've done extraordinary work, traveler. Here, you've earned this reward. And if you ever need a remedy... seek me out. I owe more than one to someone with your courage.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=16
PosMap=62
DescAudio=1557
DescFinalAudio=1558

[QUEST287]
Nombre=Living force of the Forest
Desc=Many wonder why I live up here in this old Tree House. Years ago, this place belonged to an order of druids who could listen to the forest better than anyone. I was just an apprentice when the Dry Oak Wars broke out... and when it was all over, I was the only one of my order to return to these branches. I chose to stay. The tree accepted me, and I accepted the silence of its leaves. Over time, I made this home my laboratory, where I study the vitality of the forest's creatures and how their essence can strengthen arcane magic. Since then, adventurers from Arghal and beyond have come here seeking guidance... or power. And as long as the tree stands, I will be here to aid those who know how to respect the living force of the forest. If you have come seeking power, I can help you... but nothing worthwhile comes without effort. To enhance your Magic Dart, I need materials that only Piaras Forest can provide. Three creatures guard it: the Boar, the Wild Boar, and their fearsome leader, the Alpha Boar. It is not enough to face them: you must bring me two of their horns and the Alpha's pelt. Within them resides the wild essence I need to complete my spell. Go, prove your resolve... and when you return with all that I have asked for, I will transform your magic into something far more powerful. Desde então, aventureiros de Arghal e de outros lugares vieram aqui em busca de orientação... ou poder. E enquanto a árvore estiver de pé, estarei aqui para ajudar aqueles que souberem respeitar a força vital da floresta. Se você veio em busca de poder, posso ajudá-lo... mas nada que valha a pena vem sem esforço. Para aprimorar seu Dardo Mágico, preciso de materiais que somente a Floresta de Piaras pode fornecer. Três criaturas a guardam: o Javali, o Javali Selvagem e seu temível líder, o Javali Alfa. Não basta enfrentá-los: você deve me trazer dois de seus chifres e a pele do Alfa. Neles reside a essência selvagem que preciso para completar meu feitiço. Vá, prove sua determinação... e quando retornar com tudo o que pedi, transformarei sua magia em algo muito mais poderoso.
DescFinal=Ah... Perfect! These horns still hold the primal energy of the forest, and this fur... Yes, the essence of the Alpha is strong in it. You've done admirable work. Now observe. By blending the wild vitality with your own mana, I can refine your basic spell and grant you one worthy of a true, budding mage.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=4
PosMap=157
DescAudio=1285
DescFinalAudio=1286

[QUEST288]
Nombre=Echoes of the Profane Forest
Desc=Come closer, my son... I see weariness in your eyes, but also courage. And that courage is precisely what I need to face a darkness that looms beyond these walls. Listen carefully, because what I'm about to tell you shouldn't be taken lightly. Outside the Castle lies a place that was once a living forest, a haven of peace where the wind played among the leaves and the earth breathed light. In its heart grew the sacred Araucaria de Semilla, a flower unique in all of Argentum, which, when it fell, gave life in the form of powerful Prosperous Seeds, essential for brewing the energy potions that sustain our warriors. But years ago... something profane touched that place. A dark force—the remnant of a sorcerer who defied the laws of life and death—became trapped in the forest like an open wound. Since then, the roots have become infected, the earth has cracked... and the dead have begun to rise. That forest no longer belongs to the living. Zombies patrol it like guardians of a curse they don't even understand. Their moans are nothing more than fragments of a forgotten incantation, endlessly repeating. And yet... the Araucaria endures. Wounded, yes, but clinging to its purpose. Each time it dies under the ravages of corruption, it is reborn and releases one last seed brimming with hope. Adventurer... I ask you to enter that forest. Confront the undead that infest it. Give them back the rest they were denied. And bring back some Prosperous Seeds of the Araucaria before its eternal cycle is finally broken.
DescFinal=By the gods... fifty Prosperous Seeds. I can't remember the last time someone returned with so many. The forest must have resisted your advance with fury, but you still prevailed. You have brought hope to this city, adventurer. These seeds will sustain our healers, our guardians, and perhaps... something more. I see that the echoes of the Unholy Forest failed to break you. That means you are ready to receive what I promised you. Ancient... and dangerous knowledge. Not everyone can bear this twisted blessing without being lost within it. From this moment on, you will be able to Summon Zombies. Not one of the damned of the forest, but a purified spirit, freed from the curse you yourself faced. It will not serve you out of ambition... but for balance. Remember that whoever controls a dead person also carries part of their history. Your work in the forest will not be forgotten. And if one day that place rises up against life again, I will know whom to call.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=8
PosMap=319
DescAudio=1295
DescFinalAudio=1296

[QUEST289]
Nombre=Green Lesson
Desc=Você trilhou um caminho perigoso, aprendiz. De um lado ruge Penthar, onde orcs travam sua guerra sem compreender a magia que empunham. Do outro, a Montanha Perdida guarda os ecos de minotauros caídos, orgulhosos demais para morrer em silêncio. Entre eles, apodrece esta floresta... território goblin. Eles invadem meus círculos, roubam meus componentes e profanam meus rituais. Mas eu não os odeio: eu os estudo. Seu feitiço Invocar Zumbi é mera obediência à carne morta. Eu lhe ensinarei algo superior: dominar a vontade dos vivos. Vá para a Floresta Goblin. Derrote-os. Observe-os fugir, implorar e cair. Quando estiver suficientemente subjugado, retorne à minha cabana. Então, encarando Penthar e sob a sombra da Montanha Perdida, eu reescreverei sua magia.
DescFinal=Death obeys because it has no choice. The living obey because you break their will.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=12
PosMap=186
DescAudio=1313
DescFinalAudio=1314

[QUEST290]
Nombre=The Roar that Clears the Way
Desc=This dock was once a resting place for merchants and fishermen traveling to Penthar. But something stirred the fury of the forest panthers... they no longer hunt for hunger, but for territory. My spells keep a few at bay, but the path is blocked. No one may pass. If you truly wish to strengthen your Wild Roar, prove to me that you can impose your will upon the beast. Go into the forest. Slay 15 panthers and restore calm to the path. When you return, if you are still standing, I will teach your magic to roar like never before.
DescFinal=Magic answers those who dare to face the beast and do not back down. From now on, your spell will no longer be a mere Arcane Roar.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=12
PosMap=247
DescAudio=1315
DescFinalAudio=1316

[QUEST291]
Nombre=The Heartbeat of the Ancient Fire
Desc=Centuries ago, when dragons still ruled the skies, ancient mages sealed a formidable power deep within this dungeon. The Latent Fire, a primal power that not only burns but pulses, like the heart of an ancient dragon... Within that temple dwell the Pyrrak. Humanoid beings with red scales, like glowing embers, with eyes like burning coals. They are descended from dragons, but have abandoned their winged form to walk on two legs, like monsters of fire and fury. The Pyrrak are the guardians of that power. Their bodies glow with the heat of a thousand suns, and their fury knows no bounds. If you wish to attain the Fiery Heartbeat, you must first defeat them. 30 Pyrrak, I challenge you to destroy them within their lair in the Dragon Dungeon. Only then will the Fiery Radiance resonate within you, and you will be able to summon the Fiery Heartbeat. But beware, young sorcerer… This power is not a gift, it is a curse, and those who are not worthy will burn in their own flames.
DescFinal=I can see the marks of fire on your spirit. Those humanoid creatures with red scales do not die easily... and yet, thirty of them have fallen by your hand. The fire of the Dragon Dungeon has recognized you. You are no longer a mere wielder of the Blazing Flame... now its heart beats in time with yours.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=22
PosMap=30
DescAudio=1317
DescFinalAudio=1318

[QUEST292]
Nombre=Burning Echoes of the Dead
Desc=Listen closely, traveler, for this story is never repeated. When the sun sets over Kamal and the tide recedes, the pyramid casts a shadow that points directly out to sea. This is no coincidence. It was erected to imprison that which should never rise again. Those we now call mummies were, in life, bearers of powerful magic. Upon death, their bodies were sealed with spells that still echo beneath the sand. This is why they walk... and why they guard the pyramid. Your Arcane Roar is strong, I know. You have tested it against living beasts. But within the pyramid, you will not face flesh and blood... you will face echoes. You must venture into its corridors, where the air burns and the silence weighs heavily. There, each mummy you defeat will release a fragment of ancient magic. When you have destroyed fifty, the roar will cease to be merely a voice. The sand will absorb the sound... and return it as fire. Only then will you return here. If you continue breathing, I will know that the pyramid has accepted you... and that your spell is ready to transform.
DescFinal=I don't need to ask you what you saw in there. The sand no longer clings to your shadow... and the air around you trembles. That only happens to those who have survived the trial at the pyramid. Fifty guardians of bandages and bone have fallen. With each one, an ancient voice was silenced... and another ignited within you. Listen now to your magic.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=18
PosMap=20
DescAudio=1319
DescFinalAudio=1320

[QUEST293]
Nombre=The breath that forges Ice
Desc=The power born in the North Winds has begun to shift. The ice you learned to master no longer merely shatters; it now responds. The depths where the ancient fire burns hold a test the Threshold never attempted. There, magic manifests as breath, an exhalation capable of melting spells and wills alike. Forgotten texts warn that resisting this fire means not destroying it, but understanding it. Confront this source of power and subdue its fury. In doing so, the Glacial Fracture will evolve, taking on a new form born from the clash of cold and fire—a magic that breathes and expands like a contained breath.
DescFinal=The north gave you strength. Fire gave you its breath.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=31
DescAudio=1321
DescFinalAudio=1322

[QUEST314]
Nombre=Ashes of the First Fire
Desc=Listen carefully, stranger, for I will not repeat this. The Phoenix does not always leave behind the same thing upon dying. Most of the time, only ashes and a feather plucked in combat. But on rare occasions, very rare indeed, its fire condenses into something more. An Egg. I have witnessed hundreds of rebirths from this forge, and I swear by the lava of Morgrim that barely one in a hundred leaves a complete egg. If fate smiles upon you and the Phoenix drops one upon falling, consider yourself chosen. But not everyone entrusts their future to chance. Each feather you pluck from the Phoenix holds a fragment of its rebirth. One is not enough. Nor are two. Ten feathers... from ten different deaths... together they beat like a heart of fire. Bring me ten feathers, and I will do what chance did not: I will forge a Phoenix Egg with my own hands.
DescFinal=Ten feathers, still burning. Not all come from the same rebirth. That is good. Fire needs conflict to awaken. See how they tremble, the Egg already claims form. Take it. Remember this, Firebearer: the Phoenix always rises again... and now, its fire walks with you.
Repetible=1
DescAudio=1173
DescFinalAudio=1174

[QUEST315]
Nombre=The Wings of Eternal Fire
Desc=I thought the fire would subside after the Egg... But no. The Phoenix has recognized you. Each time it falls and rises again, its wings grow stronger. They are not mere limbs... they are the symbol of its rebirth. To pluck a single feather is to defy its will. To pluck twenty... is to walk on its shadow. Listen carefully: one or ten feathers hold power, yes... but twenty feathers hold memory. The memory of every flight, every fall, every time the Phoenix chose to live again. With twenty feathers, I can forge something no dwarf has attempted since. Not true wings... but an echo of its own. Wings that will not lift you to the heavens, but will announce to all that you have survived the fire time and time again. Bring me twenty Phoenix feathers. And let the world know that the fire did not consume you.
DescFinal=Twenty feathers... Each one burned my fingers upon touching them. A good omen. See how the fire obeys... the wings remember how to burn. Take them. They won't give you flight, but they will give you presence. Wherever you walk, they will know that you defied the Phoenix twenty times... and still stand.
Repetible=1
DescAudio=1175
DescFinalAudio=1176

[QUEST317]
Nombre=The Echo of the Howls
Desc=It is not just a cave. It is a place where sanity is lost.  They call it the Cave of Desolation because everyone who enters feels something dark watching them. From its depths emerge creatures that are no longer men... but not beasts either. Ululantis, Ferus, and Laicans roam the tunnels, guided by a savage instinct that knows no rest. They were once guardians, hunters, travelers. Now only bodies twisted by the curse remain. Their howls echo through the night, and each day they draw closer to the roads that lead to the city. If we do nothing, soon there will be no safe corner left in this region. Enter the cave and eliminate as many as you can. Each creature defeated is one more life saved outside. When you have completed your task, return to me. I will reward you with gold and experience for facing the desolation that dwells in that place.
DescFinal=What you did was not just hunting beasts… it was stopping a tragedy. The presence in the cave has weakened, and for the first time in a long while, the air feels lighter. Ululantis, Ferus, and Laicans no longer dominate the tunnels as they once did. It is not a final victory, but it is a necessary one. Each creature you defeated delayed the advance of the curse and gave this land time to breathe. Take your reward. Rest, for facing desolation leaves its mark… and sooner or later, it will call again.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=16
PosMap=418
DescAudio=1256
DescFinalAudio=1257

[QUEST318]
Nombre=The Clan of the Sands
Desc=This is no isolated group, it is an entire clan. A clan of kobolds has settled in the desert, near the pyramid and the oasis. They are organized by colors, each fulfilling a role within their structure. The greys scout and keep watch, the browns dig and fortify, the blues protect the water sources, and the reds form the attacking force. As long as they act as a clan, their presence will continue to grow. They are no longer simple wandering creatures: they are claiming territory and preparing for something greater. If we do not stop them now, they will soon dominate the area around the oasis, and no traveler will be able to cross the desert safely. Go and thin their ranks. Eliminate grey, brown, blue, and red kobolds. The color does not matter: every one that falls weakens the clan’s structure. Strike them before they finish consolidating their power. When you have done your part, return to me. I will reward you with gold and experience for helping prevent this clan from becoming an unstoppable threat.
DescFinal=Well done. The clan has felt the blow. It has not been destroyed, but its organization has been weakened and its advance has been slowed. Now they know they are not alone in this desert... and that someone is willing to stand against them. Take your reward. But stay alert. As long as that clan exists near the pyramid and the oasis, they will always seek a way to regain their strength.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=14
PosMap=16
DescAudio=1208
DescFinalAudio=1209

[QUEST319]
Nombre=Contaminated energy
Desc=The swamp is alive and sick. Before the Mutant Colossus appeared, this area was dangerous, but stable. When that abomination emerged, something seeped into the earth and water. Then they came; we call them Miastrix. They didn't exist before. They are the result of the contamination left by the Colossus... creatures formed from twisted energy and swamp. Their bodies, their movements, the way they attack... everything about them responds to something we don't yet understand. I need you to eliminate 25 Miastrix, but also to observe: How do they react to combat? What does the earth do when they fall? What remains floating in the air afterward? With that information, I can condense the residual energy and create an Earth Core. I won't tell you why I'm giving it to you. I only know that the swamp responds differently when you are the one acting. And that... worries me as much as it intrigues me.
DescFinal=What you observed confirms my suspicions. The Miastrix don't move randomly. They respond to a pulse... something that remained anchored since the appearance of the Mutant Colossus. With what you brought, I was able to condense this. It's an Earthly Core. It shouldn't exist. And yet, it reacted when you thought of returning it to the swamp. That's why it's yours. Sell it if you want. Or give it to someone who knows how to listen to what it holds. Just... don't carry it around for too long.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=13
PosMap=1
DescAudio=1117
DescFinalAudio=1118

[QUEST320]
Nombre=Anomalous Resonance
Desc=I see you've brought something exceptional. That Earthly Core shouldn't be in just anyone's hands. Its energy is both powerful and delicate. If you mishandle it, it could unleash consequences neither you nor I wish to see. I need you to give it to me. I promise I won't use it for anything other than studying it. I won't move it, sell it, or destroy it: I'll only examine it to understand its nature. In return, you'll receive a reward for your time and effort. But more importantly, your discretion ensures this power doesn't fall into the wrong hands.
DescFinal=Not everyone would be prudent enough to do that. Perhaps that makes you proud... or perhaps it leaves you wondering what else could have happened.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=13
PosMap=34
DescAudio=1119
DescFinalAudio=1120

[QUEST321]
Nombre=The awakening of the Pyramid
Desc=This is no ordinary tomb. The pyramid has awakened once again. The desert sands are shifting, and with them, the creatures that lie beneath its walls. Giant scarabs crawl out from the cracks, smaller scarabs infest the corridors, and the mummies of ancient kings walk once more among the shadows. If we do not stop them now, the pyramid will become an uncontrollable nest. From there, the entire desert will be filled with wandering dead and corrupted beasts. We cannot allow that to happen. Enter the pyramid and eliminate as many as you can. Reduce their numbers before they organize. Every creature defeated is one more step toward keeping this place sealed. When you have completed your task, return to me. I will reward you with gold and experience for helping to keep the desert under control.
DescFinal=Well done. The pyramid is silent once again... for now. The advance of the creatures has been halted, and the sands rest once more. But do not let your guard down: as long as that place exists, something will always seek to escape. Take your reward. And if the pyramid stirs again, I will need your sword once more.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=18
PosMap=17
DescAudio=1121
DescFinalAudio=1122

[QUEST322]
Nombre=Purging the Forest of the Fallen
Desc=The Zombie Forests are no longer just cursed lands. They are now a direct threat to Banderbill and Nix. Patrols from both cities report that the dead are gathering far too close to the main roads. Alongside the already known Zombies, plague-corrupted dogs have appeared, mindless walkers, putrefied corpses that spread disease, and even ancient warriors who still carry their armor march endlessly among the trees. Each night they draw a little closer to the city walls. If we do not reduce their numbers now, soon there will be no way to contain them. Civilians, merchants, and supply routes will be exposed to constant attacks. Enter the Zombie Forest and eliminate as many as you can. Slow or fierce, they are all part of the same horde. Each creature destroyed is another chance for peace to remain standing. When you have completed your task, return to me. You will be rewarded with gold and experience for helping to keep the undead at bay.
DescFinal=What you did today gave the cities a moment to breathe. Patrols report that the pressure in the forest has eased and that the roads are once again passable, at least for now. The dead are still there, but their numbers are no longer as overwhelming as before. It is not a final victory, but it is a necessary one. Each zombie that fell to your weapon is one less threat to Banderbill and Nix, and one more hope for those who live behind their walls. Take your reward. The locals and merchants will not forget your help... and if the forest fills with shadows again, we will need you once more.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=13
PosMap=58
DescAudio=1123
DescFinalAudio=1124

[QUEST323]
Nombre=The Call of the Beasts
Desc=Listen carefully, Hunter. The forest doesn't respond to words, it responds to deeds. Wargs run with the fury of the wind, and grizzly bears endure like the earth itself. If you cannot face both, they will never walk beside you. You must venture deep into the forest and slay 35 wargs and 20 grizzly bears. Not out of cruelty, but so that the spirits may see that you understand their nature. Among their remains, an ancient relic may appear... a Mystic Stone. It is brown like tree bark, with veins as white as bone. This stone is not common. It forms when a beast dies defending its territory. It holds the echo of its spirit. Bring it to me. If the forest deems you worthy, the stone will choose you... and I will know you are ready.
DescFinal=The stone holds the fury of the direwolf and the resilience of the bear. It does not submit... it answers back. From now on, when you call, they will come. The direwolf will run to your side with sharp fangs, and the grizzly bear will stand firm against your enemies. Use this power with respect, Hunter. The forest watches... and never forgets.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=13
PosMap=55
DescAudio=1125
DescFinalAudio=1126

[QUEST324]
Nombre=The Seal of Ancient Fury
Desc=You have ventured where few hunters dare. South of this Elven Forest lies Pirate Island. This place was torn from the forest by violence. The spirits abandoned it... but the beasts remained. The Dire Wolves that roam the island hunt without fear or rest. They learned to kill to dominate. The Ursids withstood the chaos. They are pure strength, flesh, and fury. By slaying these creatures, a relic of the island may appear: a Mystic Rune, etched with ancient symbols and marked by salt and blood. This rune does not belong to the forest. It is the mark of what survives when the balance is broken. Journey to Pirate Island. Slay Dire Wolves and Ursids until the rune chooses you. If you return with it, I will know you are ready to summon the beasts born of chaos.
DescFinal=So the island allowed you to return... This rune was carved when the forest lost its hold on this place. It does not invoke balance. It invokes survival. The Direwolf you summon will attack relentlessly, like those that rule these shores. The Ursidae will endure where others would fall, hardened by the fury of the south. From now on, you do not summon mere beasts. You summon the spirits born when the world shattered. Use this power wisely, Hunter. Even chaos remembers those who master it.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25
PosMap=236
DescAudio=1127
DescFinalAudio=1282

[QUEST325]
Nombre=Ancient Fire Gems
Desc=I was young when I first heard this story, long before I opened my jewelry shop in this city. In those days, dragons weren't mere monsters to be hunted; they were part of the world, as ancient as magic itself. Each dragon is born bound to an element, and over the years that power condenses within. Blue Dragons fly where the cold cuts to the bone. Their breath freezes the air and the soul, and within them forms the Blue Stone, icy and silent. Red Dragons know only fury. They live among flames and ashes, and their rage never subsides. From them comes the Red Stone, hot even after the dragon's death. But Gold Dragons... they are different. They are few in number, and that is precisely why they are fearsome. They are guardians of ancient secrets, creatures who understand the value of gold better than any king. From them comes the Golden Stone, a gem capable of changing the destiny of its possessor. Listen carefully, adventurer... Don't ask why I need these stones. Nor why I'm willing to pay more gold than it's worth on any known market. There are jobs that shouldn't be done in public view, and powers that are best kept... contained.
DescFinal=Well done! Not just anyone makes it back from the Dragon Dungeon alive, let alone with these three gems intact. Here. More than I promised. These stones are worth it... and so is the risk. If you ever run into them again, you know where to bring anything that falls from their bodies.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=31
PosMap=78
DescAudio=1210
DescFinalAudio=1211

[QUEST326]
Nombre=A special order
Desc=You must help me! King Tancred will be here in town soon and Governor Conrad has commissioned me to throw a great banquet for him and his troops... But I don't have enough fishermen to feed so many, much less a King! I know there is a special fish, the Bottom Grouper... it is elusive and can be a bit of work to get, but you should be able to catch it anywhere. If you manage to do it I will reward you, please help me!
DescFinal=You saved my neck! I will be eternally grateful. If you like to get more fish, talk to me again, there will always be hungry soldiers in Nix.
RequiredLevel=1
Repetible=1
PosMap=34
DescAudio=1128
DescFinalAudio=1129

[QUEST327]
Nombre=The old Jacobo
Desc=Those damn goblins attacked my cart and stole my hooks. I'll never be able to train newbies without them! Recover them for me and show the world what it means to be a Great Angler. If you can do it, I promise to improve that old stick you call Fishing Rod with my fabulous old Jacobo technique.
DescFinal=That will teach those damn goblins not to mess with the fishing guild, excellent job!
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=14
PosMap=34
DescAudio=1163
DescFinalAudio=1164

[QUEST328]
Nombre=Mysterious Message
Desc=Have you managed to catch a mysterious bottle? Don't open it! I can offer you a great reward if you fulfill my fish order. Don't tell anyone about this!
DescFinal=If you ever catch a bottle again, don't hesitate to come back!
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=14
PosMap=254
DescAudio=1222
DescFinalAudio=1224

[QUEST329]
Nombre=Beyond the Hook
Desc=Do you really think a Reinforced Rod is enough to brave the treacherous rivers of the North? True fishing requires precision, patience... and a worthy tool. My uncle taught me the essentials, but I've taken his techniques a step further. If you want an Iron Fishing Rod, I'll need special parts. Bring that Reinforced Rod and obtain a Claw of the Azhurion. With those materials, I will forge you a rod that will not only catch fish, but tame the most stubborn fish. Do you accept the challenge?
DescFinal=There you have it: the Iron Fishing Rod. Lightweight, durable, and with a reel that won't jam even if you catch a river beast. My uncle Jacobo would say that 'fishing is patience,' but I say it's also science. Go out there and show the water who's boss.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=20
PosMap=61
DescAudio=1372
DescFinalAudio=1373

[QUEST334]
Nombre=Elemental Silks
Desc=I have dedicated much of my life to studying ancient arcane techniques capable of creating fabrics imbued with elemental energy. According to my research, the silks produced by the Elemental Spiders of the Catacombs possess unique properties when combined correctly. Ancient chronicles tell of how, using fibers from the four elements, it is possible to create an extremely light and strong thread. With this material, in ancient times, fabrics were woven that were linked to magical and legendary creatures. Among these legends appears the Unicorn... a mystical creature that only manifests itself to those who possess a special connection to elemental magic. If I wish to verify if these stories are true, I must first gather a vast quantity of elemental silks. That is why I need your help, adventurer. You must venture into the depths of the Catacombs and hunt the Elemental Spiders that dwell there. Each one produces a silk infused with the power of its element. Yes... I need one hundred of each. Only with that quantity will I be able to work properly with the energies of the four elements.
DescFinal=I see you've returned... and not empty-handed. Let me see those silks... Incredible. The elemental energy they contain is even purer than I expected. With an amount like this, I can finally begin my work at the loom. Weaving together the essences of water, fire, wind, and earth is no easy task, but if the ancient legends are true, this will be the first step toward creating a material worthy of the most magical creatures that have ever existed. You've done a great job, adventurer. Take this: it's Amida Light Thread. It's just the beginning of something much greater... and perhaps, if the stories are to be believed, also the first step toward the mystery of the Unicorn.
Repetible=1
PosMap=1
DescAudio=1046
DescFinalAudio=1047

[QUEST335]
Nombre=The Arcane Loom
Desc=Arkhavel has taken the first step by creating the Light Amida Thread, but now the real challenge begins. To weave a fabric capable of holding ancient magic, I must work for days at my arcane loom. However, to accomplish this, I need a vast quantity of this material. If you truly wish to continue this project, you must bring me a large supply of Light Amida Thread. Only with that amount can I attempt to weave something few have seen in centuries: a Unicorn Canvas.
DescFinal=This is... extraordinary. I never thought I'd see so many Lightweight Amida Yarns gathered in one place. Weaving this material hasn't been easy, but the result speaks for itself. Elemental energy flows through every fiber of the fabric. This is the Unicorn Canvas. According to ancient legends, fabrics like this were used in rituals to attract and bind creatures of magical purity. If the old tales are true... this canvas could be the key to encountering one of them.
Repetible=1
PosMap=151
DescAudio=1078
DescFinalAudio=1079

[QUEST336]
Nombre=Unicorn Bond
Desc=The Unicorn Canvas you wear is unique, woven with pure elemental energies and ancient techniques almost forgotten by mortals. According to legend, only those who have demonstrated patience, dedication, and respect for the world's magic can approach a Unicorn. This canvas is not merely a fabric; it is a conduit for the energy of these creatures, capable of attracting them and binding them to a worthy rider. If you wish to walk alongside a Unicorn and share its power, you must give it to me. In return, you will receive the Unicorn Mount, a noble and magical being that will answer your call.
DescFinal=Take good care of it, adventurer, for only those who honor the magic of the world can maintain its trust.
Repetible=1
PosMap=517
DescAudio=1080
DescFinalAudio=1081

[QUEST339]
Nombre=The Flame of Heroism
Desc=Within the Temple of the Paladins lies an ancient ritual reserved only for those who demonstrate discipline, willpower, and mastery of combat: the Rite of Heroism. This rite is not a gift or an immediate blessing; it is a test. Centuries ago, the temple's sages discovered that certain creatures and plants of the world contain a natural essence capable of awakening a warrior's physical potential. Not just anyone can gather these components: they must be obtained through effort, combat, and determination. Only then does the ritual work.
DescFinal=The ritual is complete. Your will will be the spark.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=25
DescAudio=1086
DescFinalAudio=1087

[QUEST340]
Nombre=The Islands Dispute
Desc=The islands of New Hope and the Elven Forest are no longer what they once were. Ancient forces have awakened, and with them, creatures that have lost all sense of reason. In the heart of the forest, the Elven Ent has been corrupted. Its fury distinguishes no friend from foe, and all who approach are attacked without mercy. Further afield, on the shores of New Hope, a colossal beast known as Gigantor has emerged. Its wake is marked by destruction, and its presence threatens to erase any attempt at control over the island. But you are not the only one who has been sent. Soldiers from both factions march to these lands with the same objective: to prevail, to dominate the region... and to claim glory. Your mission is clear. Head to one of the contested islands. Hold your position. Defend the territory from those who would seize it... and when the time comes, confront the creature that dwells there. It will not be easy. These entities resurface over time, as if the land itself refuses to let them disappear. If you manage to defeat them and prove your loyalty in battle, you will be rewarded with a Potion of Factional Honor, proof of your courage and commitment. Remember this, soldier: here you don't just fight monsters... you fight for the honor of your faction. And only those who stand firm will be remembered.
DescFinal=The banners of your faction fly higher than ever. Your victory has not gone unnoticed. Messengers already carry news of your feat, and your name begins to resonate among your people as a symbol of determination and loyalty. You have proven that, even in contested territories, your will is stronger than any threat. In recognition, you receive a Potion of Factional Honor.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=25
DescAudio=1298
DescFinalAudio=1299

[QUEST341]
Nombre=Subjugate the Warrior
Desc=You have tamed beasts and lesser creatures, but orcs are another story. They do not bend easily: their will is tempered in war, blood, and endurance. If you aspire to summon them, you must prove that your magic can prevail even over that which scorns submission. Venture into their domain, confront them without hesitation, and break their spirit. Only when you have subdued enough, return to me.
DescFinal=Might prevails where reason cannot!
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=16
PosMap=69
DescAudio=1311
DescFinalAudio=1312

[QUEST380]
Nombre=Dolgrin's Offering
Desc=The four elements are not to be mastered. They are to be gathered. Since the dwarves of Morgrim deciphered the language of essences, they have known that fire, earth, wind and water are not separate forces: they are fragments of the same ancient power. Dolgrin has spent years waiting for those capable of forging what few dare to bring together. Bring me ten Elemental Runes of each element and I will give you something that cannot be found anywhere else in the known world.
DescFinal=The runes have found their form. The chest is yours... for now. But the elements never stop flowing, and Dolgrin never stops waiting. If one day you gather enough again, you know where to find me.
Repetible=1
PosMap=591
DescAudio=1574
DescFinalAudio=1575

[QUEST385]
Nombre=Reduce the Forces
Desc=Soldier! The Legion Guards who protect Arkhein wear a red and black bracelet, a symbol of their oath to the Legion. If you managed to take that bracelet from them, it would be a direct blow to their morale and a victory for the Kingdom. It won't be easy ? they don't give it up without a fight... but if fortune favors you, one of them will drop it. Bring it to me, and the Kingdom will reward you with a Faction Points Potion. For the Honor of the Kingdom!
DescFinal=I knew it. I knew you could do it. This bracelet is much more than an object ? it is proof that the Legion's forces are not invincible. The Kingdom does not forget those who fight for it. Here is your reward, well earned.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=25
DescAudio=1304
DescFinalAudio=1305

[QUEST386]
Nombre=Reduce the Forces
Desc=Listen carefully. The Royal Guards of Banderbill wear a blue bracelet, a mark of their servitude to the corrupt monarch who oppresses these lands. Taking that bracelet from them is not just an act of war... it's a message. A message that no one who serves that king is safe. It won't fall easily ? you'll have to fight and wait for the shadow to favor you. But if you manage it, I will reward you with a Faction Points Potion. The shadow will guide you.
DescFinal=Well done. This blue bracelet, which they once wore with such pride, is now in the hands of the Legion. That is exactly what we needed. Your loyalty does not go unnoticed. Take your reward.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=25
DescAudio=1300
DescFinalAudio=1301

[QUEST390]
Nombre=The Watcher of the Depths
Desc=If you've made it this far, I assume you're not afraid of the Underworld. But there's something you should know before you go any farther. Bael, the Fire Leviathan, relentlessly patrols the entrance to the underground depths, turning the path into a death sentence for the reckless. More than one warrior tried to face it head-on... and none lived to tell the tale. The only way to bring these beasts down is by keeping your distance. If you've mastered the bow, magic, or any other ranged attack, you'll be able to strike before its flames consume you. While the Underworld remains open, we must reduce their numbers so other adventurers have a chance to descend into the depths alive. Go and slay 20 Bael using only ranged attacks. Return to me when you're done, and you'll be rewarded for your service to all who dare challenge the Underworld.
DescFinal=You've proven your patience, precision, and the resolve needed to survive the Underworld. Here is the reward I promised. You've earned it.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=36
DescAudio=1594
DescFinalAudio=1595

[QUEST391]
Nombre=The Spore Plague
Desc=South of Forgat lies a place few dare to tread: the Isle of Spores. For years it was fertile land, but today the air is thick with a poisonous dust that gives life to monstrous fungi. Niscalos, Bisporus and Amanitas have grown feeding on these toxins, becoming creatures as resilient as they are lethal. Each species hides a different poison. Some release spores that numb the body, others slowly poison their prey, and the most dangerous can cause hallucinations before they attack. The wind is starting to carry these spores toward Forgat, and if the plague keeps spreading, it will soon reach the fields and roads near the city. Travel to the Isle of Spores and cull their numbers before it's too late. Once you've eliminated enough creatures, return to me. You will be rewarded for protecting Forgat from this silent threat.
DescFinal=The spores still drift through the air, but no longer with the same intensity. The fungal colony has taken a heavy blow, and for now its spread has stopped. The roads south of Forgat are a bit safer again for travelers and merchants. We won't be able to fully wipe out the plague while the island remains contaminated, but your intervention has bought us the time we needed. Accept your reward. And remember... on the Isle of Spores, even what seems dead can grow again.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=25
PosMap=289
DescAudio=1521
DescFinalAudio=1522

[QUEST392]
Nombre=The Fury of the Depths
Desc=The waters surrounding the Abandoned City are no longer safe. In its depths, an ancient being has awakened: Zeraphon, the Leviathan, whose roar shakes the currents and whose fury drags down all who dare cross its path. Far to the east, beneath the turquoise waters, lies the Coral Reef, a submerged dungeon where Kaelthor, the Naga King, rules with an iron fist over his court of marine creatures. Both factions have received the same order: descend into the depths, face these titans of the sea, and return with proof of their victory. It will not be an easy task. Zeraphon and Kaelthor are no simple beasts: they are ancient guardians who resurface time and again, as if the ocean itself refuses to let them die. Whoever manages to defeat both, proving mettle and loyalty to their faction, will be rewarded with a Potion of Factional Honor. Remember, soldier: the sea shows no mercy to the weak, but rewards those who dare to challenge it in the name of their banner.
DescFinal=The depths have been conquered. Zeraphon and Kaelthor lie defeated, and with them falls the myth of their invincibility. Sailors of your faction already recount the feat in the ports, and your name joins the list of those who dared to challenge the sea and returned alive. In recognition of your bravery, you receive a Potion of Factional Honor.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=27
DescAudio=1483
DescFinalAudio=1484

[QUEST406]
Nombre=The Four Nests
Desc=Not everyone makes it this far. The key that unlocks the Lower Catacombs has remained hidden for years, and those who have crossed its gates speak of a chamber where nature itself seems to have been corrupted. Deep below dwell four ancient species of spiders, each bound to a primordial element. Gale commands the winds, Tellus shakes the earth, Blaze devours everything with its flames, and Nevora turns water into a deadly weapon. Individually they are dangerous
DescFinal=The four colonies have suffered a devastating blow, and activity within the second level of the Catacombs has diminished considerably. The air has grown still once more, the earth no longer trembles, the flames burn less fiercely, and the flooded tunnels have regained a calm they had long since lost. The elemental forces still linger in the depths, and sooner or later new creatures will claim the abandoned nests. For now, however, the balance has been restored, and those who dare venture into these ruins stand a far greater chance of returning alive. You have proven yourself worthy of overcoming one of the Catacombs' greatest challenges. Take your reward.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=13
DescAudio=1466
DescFinalAudio=1467

[QUEST407]
Nombre=A New Adventure
Desc=Welcome, Adventurer! You look strong. Perhaps you can help us bring better times back to this town. For some time now, different pests have begun appearing around Forgat. Snakes, rats, red ants, and other creatures have settled north of the city, making the roads and nearby fields increasingly dangerous. If you are willing, help us clear some of the area north of the city. We cannot offer you much, but the townspeople have gathered some gold to reward anyone willing to lend us a hand. It may not be a glorious task, but every great adventurer has to start somewhere.
DescFinal=Thank you! Thank you, Adventurer! You have done a great job. The creatures that once roamed north of Forgat no longer pose a threat to those who venture beyond the city. It may seem like a small thing, but every effort counts. With your help and that of other adventurers, we can begin clearing the surrounding areas and slowly rebuild our town. We do not have much to offer you, but we keep our word. Remember that Forgat will always have work for those willing to help.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=1
DescAudio=1469
DescFinalAudio=1470

[QUEST408]
Nombre=Land of Predators
Desc=Hello again, Adventurer. I have an urgent message from the houses east of the city. Apparently, a pack of wolves led by an alpha has begun attacking the animals in the area, making the local wildlife increasingly aggressive. Ostriches, crows, and other beasts that would normally avoid the inhabitants have become dangerous, even approaching the houses to the south. The villagers are terrified and fear that, if the pack continues to grow, the attacks may eventually reach Forgat. Go east of the forest and find out what is causing this behavior. If you find the leader of the pack, eliminate him and put an end to this threat before the situation gets worse.
DescFinal=You have done well, Adventurer. The pack has lost its leader, and with him, the fury that seemed to have taken hold of the beasts is beginning to fade. The ostriches have once again moved away from the houses, and the crows no longer attack those who approach the forest. For now, the families in the south can breathe easy. However, something does not quite add up. Animals do not usually behave this way without a reason. Perhaps the alpha was simply defending its territory... or perhaps something else was driving it to act this way. In any case, you have fulfilled your task. Take your reward and remain vigilant. The forest is peaceful once again, but we do not know how long it will last.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=3
DescAudio=1471
DescFinalAudio=1472

[QUEST409]
Nombre=Outlaw
Desc=North of Forgat, the roads have begun to become dangerous. Travelers and merchants have reported increasingly frequent attacks, and some of them have never returned. At first, it was believed to be the work of simple bandits, but recent reports tell a different story. The attackers are well armed, move in groups, and seem far too organized to be mere thieves. Their presence also appears to have disturbed the region. The packs of gray wolves that inhabit the nearby forests have become extremely aggressive, attacking hunters and even those traveling along the roads. Travel north of Forgat and eliminate the mercenaries you find in the area. Also hunt down the wolves that have become a threat to travelers. Once you have reduced their numbers sufficiently, return to me. You will be rewarded for restoring safety to the roads.
DescFinal=The mercenaries have suffered a heavy blow, and the wolves that once preyed on travelers and merchants no longer pose the same threat. For now, those who must cross the northern lands of Forgat can do so without fearing an ambush at every turn. Mercenaries this well equipped do not appear in a region by chance. Someone hired them, and until we know who was behind it and what they were truly seeking, we cannot consider this matter closed. For now, you have done your part. Take your reward.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=5
DescAudio=1473
DescFinalAudio=1474

[QUEST410]
Nombre=Dark Retribution
Desc=We have a new problem, Adventurer, and this time it is not a matter of simple beasts. Several travelers have been found dead on the roads east of Forgat. They were not attacked by animals. Their wounds indicate that they were murdered by armed men, and the few witnesses who managed to escape speak of groups of assassins hiding among the ruins in the area. But that is not the worst of it. Skeletons have begun appearing alongside the bodies. They are not the remains of ancient inhabitants of Forgat
DescFinal=You have returned alive. That is already more than many can say. The assassins have been eliminated, and the skeletons that once roamed the roads have returned to where they belong: beneath the earth. But there is something we cannot ignore. Those skeletons did not belong to these lands. Someone brought them here from another region and raised them through necromancy. And if a group of necromancers is going to such lengths to send the dead to Forgat, there must be a reason. Take your reward. And remember, Adventurer... when the dead begin to walk, they rarely do so without someone guiding them.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=7
DescAudio=1475
DescFinalAudio=1476

[QUEST411]
Nombre=The Corrupted Altar
Desc=We have troubling news, Adventurer. North of the city stands an ancient altar that was once a place of rest and pilgrimage. No one has used it for a long time, but it still retained a small amount of divine energy, enough to keep the place protected from dark forces. That has changed. The necromancers' forces have reached the altar and begun using it for their own purposes. They have raised corpses from the surrounding area and turned them into zombies, slowly corrupting the last traces of divine energy that remained in the place. The corruption has also affected the creatures of the region. Even the turtles that once lived near the altar have begun to rot, transforming into aggressive and deformed creatures. If we allow the altar to become completely corrupted, we do not know what kind of power the necromancers could obtain. Travel to the altar and eliminate the zombies and rotting zombies found there. Also destroy the decaying turtles and cleanse the area of every creature affected by the corruption.
DescFinal=You have managed to cleanse the altar. The dead that once walked among the ruins have fallen silent once again, and the corrupted creatures that infested the surrounding area no longer pose a threat. But I fear we arrived too late to completely save this place. The divine energy that remained within the altar has been almost destroyed. What little remains can barely be felt, like a flame on the verge of going out. The necromancers were not merely raising the dead. They are searching for places where even a trace of power still exists and corrupting it for their own purposes. This confirms our worst fears. What happened at the altar was not an isolated attack. The necromancers are advancing, and if they continue this way, Forgat may not be their true target... but merely the beginning. Take your reward, Adventurer. And if you find another sacred place in danger, do not wait until the last flame goes out.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=9
DescAudio=1477
DescFinalAudio=1478

[QUEST412]
Nombre=The Cursed Lair
Desc=We have finally found the source of it all. For weeks, the necromancers have spread their influence across the lands surrounding Forgat. They raised the dead, corrupted the ancient altar, and sent assassins to eliminate anyone who might uncover their plans. Now we know where they are hiding. Their lair lies far from the roads, hidden among the ruins of an ancient structure. A race known as the Scrammers has gathered there, creatures who have embraced the dark arts and serve a mysterious leader known simply as the Elder. The lair is protected by numerous servants. Some are mere Scrammers, while others have learned to move through the shadows and strike without warning. There are also hooded figures who appear to be directly involved in the rituals taking place within the lair. But the true danger is the Elder. The few accounts we have managed to gather speak of a being who possesses dark powers far greater than those of his followers. We do not know how long he has been there or what he intends to accomplish, but everything that has happened so far seems to lead directly to him. The time has come to put an end to this.
DescFinal=You have done it. The Scrammers' lair has been destroyed and their forces have been defeated. The dead have stopped rising and, for the first time in a long while, the darkness spreading around Forgat appears to have been halted. The surviving Scrammers have fled, abandoning the ruins and leaving behind the remains of their rituals. But the Elder... His presence was different. The power he wielded was unlike that of the others. Even after everything that has happened, it is difficult to believe that someone like him could have acquired such knowledge on his own. The skeletons, the murders, the corrupted altar... it was all part of something. And although we have destroyed their lair, far too many questions remain unanswered. Where did the Scrammers learn to manipulate these forces? Who taught the Elder? And how many other places were corrupted before we arrived? For now, Forgat can breathe easy. You have completed a mission that few would have accepted. Take your reward, Adventurer. But do not forget what you saw inside. The darkness has been defeated, but not necessarily destroyed.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=11
DescAudio=1479
DescFinalAudio=1480

[QUEST413]
Nombre=The Legacy of Shadows
Desc=East of Penthar stands a structure that remained empty and forgotten for years. However, those who have recently ventured near it claim to have seen movement in its windows and strange shadows wandering through its halls. The so-called Abandoned Hideout has two levels. The first is inhabited by Demonic Henchmen and Demonic Henchwomen, along with numerous Specters, creatures that seem to be guarding something hidden deep within the ruins. But the true threat lies on the second floor. There dwell two powerful gargoyles, Zevkar and Gorath, who have claimed the ancient chambers as their territory. No one knows how long they have been there or what purpose they serve. The people of Penthar fear that these creatures are secretly preparing something. As long as they remain inside the hideout, no one can venture there without putting their life at risk. Enter the Abandoned Hideout and eliminate the Demonic Henchmen, Demonic Henchwomen, Specters, and the gargoyles Zevkar and Gorath. Explore both floors and make sure none of these creatures continue to lurk among the ruins. When you are finished, return to me. The people of Penthar will be able to sleep peacefully once again knowing that the hideout is no longer under the control of these creatures.
DescFinal=The Abandoned Hideout has fallen silent. The Demonic Henchmen and Demonic Henchwomen no longer roam its corridors, the Specters have vanished from their ancient chambers, and the gargoyles that ruled the second floor have been defeated. Zevkar and Gorath will no longer watch over the ruins from above, and for the first time in a long while, the abandoned halls have ceased to serve as a refuge for demonic creatures. We do not know what truly happened within those walls or why so many creatures gathered there, but as long as the ruins remain silent, Penthar will be safe from their threat. You have done your part. Take your reward.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=25
DescAudio=1597
DescFinalAudio=1598
PosMap=461

[QUEST414]
Nombre=The Mutiny of the Southern Isle
Desc=South of Kamal, where the desert meets the sea, a small island has become the refuge of a crew of renegade pirates. What began as a mutiny has turned into a band of ruthless raiders who ambush merchant ships and coastal caravans before vanishing among the island's cliffs. The Insurgent Pirates and Mutinous Pirates patrol the area without allegiance to any flag, spreading fear among fishermen, sailors, and merchants alike. If no one intervenes, the sea routes that supply Kamal will soon fall under the control of these outlaws. Travel to the island and defeat enough Insurgent Pirates and Mutinous Pirates to break the strength of the rebel crew. Return to me once your task is complete. You will be rewarded for restoring safety to Kamal's shores.
DescFinal=The pirates' activity has diminished considerably. The waters around the island are once again safer to navigate, allowing merchant vessels to travel with far less fear. While new outlaws may one day take the place of those who fell, this crew is no longer a serious threat to Kamal. Your victory has reopened an important trade route between the desert and the sea, bringing stability back to those who depend on it. Accept your reward. You have proven that even the fiercest pirates can be brought down.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=25
DescAudio=1481
DescFinalAudio=1482
PosMap=17

[QUEST415]
Nombre=The Children of the Tides
Desc=If you have made it this far, then you have already seen the ruins hidden beneath the waters of the Coral Reef. But what lies beyond this entrance is unlike anything that inhabits our seas. Long ago, an ancient race made its home in the depths. Its members are known as the Children of the Tides, beings half warrior and half sea creature who learned to survive where no man could. For years they remained hidden among the reefs and submerged caverns. Now they have begun to spread through the depths, and their scouts are venturing closer and closer to the waters crossed by our ships. Kadru and Lynn lead their warriors, while Aksha and Varec hold positions of greater importance within their strange hierarchy. Each appears to guard a part of the ancient caverns they inhabit. We do not know what they seek or why they have begun to abandon their domains. The only thing we know is that their presence has become too dangerous to ignore. Enter the underwater cave and face the Children of the Tides. Defeat their warriors and bring down those who hold the highest positions within their hierarchy. If you manage to return alive, you will have proven that the depths of the Coral Reef are not a place reserved solely for its inhabitants.
DescFinal=The waters are calm once again. The warriors who guarded the depths have fallen, and those who led the Children of the Tides can no longer continue expanding their domain. Kadru, Lynn, Aksha, and Varec have been defeated, but their caverns still hold secrets that we may never fully understand. The ruins beneath the reef are far older than any known settlement, and if this race survived there for so long, they were surely not the first inhabitants of those depths. For now, however, the waters once again belong to those brave enough to sail them. You have returned from a place few manage to escape. That deserves a reward.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=27
DescAudio=1601
DescFinalAudio=1602
PosMap=478

[QUEST416]
Nombre=The Protection of the Insects
Desc=I have been studying the assassin mantises that inhabit these lands. Their exoskeletons possess properties that could be used to create a tunic unlike any other, but I will need a large quantity of materials to complete my work. The brown assassin mantises possess strong and flexible plates, ideal for reinforcing the tunic's inner lining. Their structure will help protect the wearer without turning the garment into heavy armor. On the other hand, the green assassin mantises have a coloration and outer structure that are especially useful for crafting the surface of the garment. Their parts will be used for the outer layer, improving the wearer's visibility in forested areas and providing an additional layer of protection. I will need enough parts from both species before I can begin crafting. It will not be an easy task, but if you gather the necessary materials, I will create a unique tunic for you.
DescFinal=Excellent work. You have gathered enough pieces from the assassin mantises. Here is your reward: a unique tunic, crafted from the exoskeletons of assassin mantises. May it protect you as well as they once protected their territory.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=15
PosMap=1
DescAudio=1464
DescFinalAudio=1465

[QUEST417]
Nombre=The Last Message
Desc=You found a sealed bottle drifting among the waves. Inside was a surprisingly well-preserved parchment. "If anyone finds this message, know that it was not the storm that doomed us. The waters surrounding the continent no longer belong to mankind. Leviathans rise from the depths, Sharks stalk every vessel daring enough to cross these seas, Sirens lure sailors into the depths with their songs, and strange creatures we came to call Cryptococci infest the remains of shipwrecks. One by one, my crew fell. If these beasts are not stopped, the sea will cease to be a passage and become a grave." I do not know how long this bottle has been drifting, but if that captain spoke the truth, the danger still remains. Sail into the open sea and reduce the number of these creatures before more lives are lost. When you have completed your mission, go to map 254 and speak with Fermín, the fisherman. I'm afraid he knows something about this matter.
DescFinal=Ha... the old bottle fulfilled its purpose. What? You didn't know? Long ago, I was a daring captain who sailed these seas. But I never believed that message would ever reach anyone. Especially not after so many decades. The Leviathans, Sharks, Sirens, and Cryptococci have suffered heavy losses, and the sea routes are once again a little safer for fishermen, merchants, and travelers. The danger has not disappeared. As long as the depths endure, there will always be monsters lurking beneath the waves. But today, thanks to you, the continent can breathe a little easier. Take this reward.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=25
DescAudio=1294
DescFinalAudio=1442
PosMap=254

[QUEST418]
Nombre=Purification of the Sanctuary
Desc=These ancient pages bear the seal of the Dungeon Veril sanctuary, and still carry traces of the dark magic that once surrounded them. The text tells how the Medusa, corrupted by the shadows, seized this sacred book from the hands of the guardians and hid it in her lair, guarding it with her petrifying gaze. Only by defeating her is there a chance to recover it among her remains. The pages also speak of the Witches, who poisoned the sacred waters with their rituals, and of the Stone Golems, risen to seal the entrance and prevent anyone from ever returning. At the end, a warning: "Only one who slays these creatures can free Dungeon Veril from its curse. Bring these pages back to Phenoba, in the city of Arghal, and let the light guide this sanctuary once more."
DescFinal=You have returned... and you bring with you what we so desperately needed. The Medusa, the Witches, and the Stone Golems will no longer cast their shadow over Dungeon Veril. This book confirms it: the sanctuary can breathe in peace once again. You have shown a courage few possess, traveler. Take this reward, you have earned it well, and may my magic accompany you in every battle you wage from now on.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=33
PosMap=171
DescAudio=1038
DescFinalAudio=1293

[QUEST419]
Nombre=The Fragment of the Four
Desc=You have found a strange fragment among the remains of a defeated creature. At first glance, it appears to be a dark stone, but upon closer inspection, you can make out four symbols engraved on its surface: an ant, a wolf, a dragon, and a creature shrouded in shadows. An ancient inscription runs along the edge of the fragment: "Four realms. Four lords. Four forces that should never have shared the same symbol." The inscription seems to refer to four creatures that rule over very different territories. Gaia, the Queen of Ants, rules from the depths of the Ant Colony and commands a colony capable of devouring anything that invades its territory. Laican, the Alpha Wolf, has established his domain in the Cave of Desolation. No creature dares to challenge him within his caverns. Nocthral remains hidden in the depths of the Dragon Dungeon, where his presence has turned the ancient corridors into a deadly territory. And in Marabel Dungeon awaits Escarlath, a creature whose influence has transformed the depths of that place into his own kingdom. The strangest thing is that the fragment seems to react to the names of all four. Perhaps each of them possesses a part of the same power. Find Gaia, Laican, Nocthral, and Escarlath and defeat them. If the inscription speaks the truth, defeating these four rulers could reveal the true purpose of the fragment. When you have completed your mission, go and speak with Krazgor on map 189. Perhaps then we can discover what connection exists between these four rulers.
DescFinal=The fragment has returned to your hands following the fall of the four rulers. Gaia no longer rules the Ant Colony, Laican has lost his dominion over the Cave of Desolation, Nocthral has been defeated in the depths of the Dragon Dungeon, and Escarlath no longer reigns over the dark galleries of Marabel. When the marks of the four rulers were brought together on the fragment, the symbols began to glow and an ancient inscription appeared on its surface: "When four realms fall, the path shall once again be open." We do not know what path the inscription refers to, nor who created this strange object. Perhaps the four rulers were chosen for a reason we have yet to understand. What we do know is that you have defeated four of the most powerful creatures that ruled over different regions of the continent. For completing your mission, take your reward.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=13
DescAudio=888
DescFinalAudio=908
PosMap=189

[QUEST420]
Nombre=The Moon Shard
Desc=Among the charred remains of a fallen adventurer, you find a desperate note: "If you're reading this, it's because the red dragon caught me before I caught it. I was searching for the Moon Shard for Bertram, the jeweler of Arghal, who pays well for stones no ordinary craftsman can carve. According to my research, it's the black dragon of the dark swamps who guards it in its jaws, though you'll also have to face the red dragon of the valleys of fire and the golden one of the sacred summit, as none of the three tolerate intruders in their domains. If you have the courage I lacked, kill them, get the stone from the black one, and bring it to Bertram in my name."
DescFinal=This stone... is no ordinary gem. I'll need to study it more closely. If this is what I suspect, I may need your services again soon.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=31
PosMap=151

[QUEST421]
Nombre=Echoes of the Ice
Desc=As soon as you take the skull in your hands, the symbols carved into the bone light up with a cold, bluish glow. A chill that has nothing to do with the weather runs through your body, and for a moment you think you hear a guttural whisper, as if something long dormant had awakened at your touch. The skull crumbles into frosted dust, but the sensation remains: you now know the Ghoul was nothing more than a sentinel, one of many guardians protecting something far more ancient within the Frozen Cavern. To understand what truly lies hidden beneath the ice, you'll need to face the other creatures that guard its depths: the Eyewarden, whose frozen gaze can paralyze any intruder
DescFinal=The ice holds more secrets than most dare to seek.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=29
PosMap=354
DescAudio=1021
DescFinalAudio=1035

[QUEST422]
Nombre=The Heart of the Underworld
Desc=The Underworld has opened its gates once again, although only for a few hours. Deep within its depths dwell creatures that carry a powerful essence of fire, and ancient tales claim that they are all connected to an elemental source known as the Heart of the Underworld. Venture into its domains and defeat Flamoras, Astaroths, Pyrrions, Phyrus, Gran Blazes, Fire Mantises, and Baels. Perhaps by defeating enough of these creatures, we can weaken the force that keeps the heart of this place burning.
DescFinal=The creatures of fire have fallen, and for a brief moment, the flames of the Underworld seem to have weakened. Their fiery essence has dissipated throughout the depths, as if something far more ancient were losing its strength. We do not know where the Heart of the Underworld lies or what will happen when it regains its power. But you have managed to disturb the balance of the depths and survived one of the most dangerous places on the continent. For completing your mission, take your reward.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=36
DescAudio=1019
DescFinalAudio=1020

[QUEST423]
Nombre=The Decree of the Guardians
Desc=You have found an ancient scroll sealed with an emblem that no one recognizes anymore. The ink has faded with the passage of time, but the message remains intact. "To every adventurer capable of reading these words: the balance of the continent depends on the fall of four guardians whose existence has altered the course of the world. Gigantor rules over New Hope Island with a strength capable of bringing down fortresses. The Ice Giant slays anyone who dares to set foot in the North Pole. Zeraphon rules the Leviathan Sea, turning those waters into a graveyard for sailors. And the Elven Ent protects the heart of the Elven Forest, where the roots answer only to its will. As long as these four colossi remain standing, no corner of the continent will ever be truly safe. If you possess the necessary strength, find them and put an end to their reign." There is no record of who wrote this decree or how many attempted to fulfill it. The only certainty is that very few have been capable of facing even one of these beings. Defeat the four world bosses and prove that you are worthy of completing a feat reserved for the most powerful adventurers. Then, go and speak with Sheila on map 171 to claim your reward.
DescFinal=The four guardians have fallen and, for the first time in centuries, their domains have fallen silent. As I examine the scroll, I can make out a small inscription hidden beneath the seal: "Four have fallen. The balance may begin to be restored." I do not know who wrote these words or why these four colossi were chosen. Perhaps their defeat is part of something far older than we can imagine. You have fulfilled your mission. Take your reward.
Repetible=1
RequiredLevel=25
DescAudio=918
DescFinalAudio=1017

[QUEST424]
Nombre=Beyond Ensnare
Desc=You have learned to use Ensnare, but this spell is only the beginning. There is a much more powerful magic: Stun. Brumaks know this spell well and use it to leave their enemies immobile. If you want to master it, you will have to face them and prove that you can withstand their power. However, they will not be your only challenge
DescFinal=You have done it. You have learned to take the power of Ensnare much further. Now you will be able to leave your enemies completely immobile. Master Stun and let them learn the true meaning of paralysis.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=24
PosMap=560
DescAudio=852
DescFinalAudio=853

[QUEST425]
Nombre=The Art of Invisibility
Desc=Invisibility is a complex art that few can master completely. Hiding the body is simple
DescFinal=You have learned to control the forces that allow you to disappear completely from sight. Your former mastery of invisibility is now behind you, and you are capable of using a much more powerful version of the spell. Few know the secrets of this technique, and even fewer are capable of mastering it. Take this knowledge and use it wisely.
Repetible=0
PosMap=354
DescAudio=793
DescFinalAudio=794
RequiredLevel=0

[QUEST426]
Nombre=The Art of Invisibility (Semi-Magical)
Desc=Invisibility is a complex art that few can master completely. Hiding the body is simple
DescFinal=You have learned to control the forces that allow you to disappear completely from sight. Your former mastery of invisibility is now behind you, and you are capable of using a much more powerful version of the spell. Few know the secrets of this technique, and even fewer are capable of mastering it. Take this knowledge and use it wisely.
Repetible=0
PosMap=354
DescAudio=795
DescFinalAudio=801
RequiredLevel=0

[QUEST427]
Nombre=A Small Rat Problem
Desc=Near Makrom you will find two rats prepared for this quest. Defeat them and wait for them to respawn until you complete 5 kills. Use the Journal to track your progress and pin the objective. When you are done, return to Makrom to claim the reward.
DescFinal=Well done. You have learned the full quest cycle: accept a task, track it in the Journal, pin the objective, complete it, and return for the reward. This is only the beginning of your adventure.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=1
DescAudio=714
DescFinalAudio=720

[QUEST900]
Nombre=Cenizas del Primer Fuego
Desc=Traeme 10 Plumas de Fenix y te entregare un Huevo de Fenix, que guarda el poder ancestral de las llamas.
DescFinal=Las cenizas guardan su poder. Aqui tienes tu Huevo de Fenix.
RequiredLevel=1
Repetible=1

[QUEST901]
Nombre=Las Alas del Fuego Eterno
Desc=Reune 20 Plumas de Fenix y forjare para ti unas Alas de Fenix, simbolo del fuego eterno.
DescFinal=El fuego eterno te acompana. Lleva con orgullo tus Alas de Fenix.
RequiredLevel=1
Repetible=0

[QUEST902]
Nombre=The Jewelry of the Element
Desc=Thirga Brumhilda looks you up and down, weighing whether you have the patience for the forge's finest work. "Fire forges steel," she says, "but elemental jewelcrafting demands something more: the four pure essences. Fire, Water, Earth and Wind, each torn from a beast that guards them with its life. Bring me one of each, plus 800,000 gold coins for the fine materials, and I will teach you to set them in gold and silver. No shortcuts, Worker: whoever rushes jewelcrafting ends up with burned hands."
DescFinal=Ha! The four essences, intact, in your hand. Few endure the hunt needed to gather them all. Now pay attention: setting an orb, a ring or an amulet is not forging a sword, it is listening to the element before you lock it into the metal. From today, that listening is yours. Use the recipe with your head, and may your jewelcraft outlast your forge!
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=33
PosMap=594

[QUEST903]
Nombre=The Master's Distillate
Desc="Anyone can drop a flower into a flask," she says, pointing at a row of gleaming oils. "But the Superior oil, the one that truly makes a difference in combat, needs all four Refined oils at once, plus 500,000 gold coins to pay for the rare reagents. Bring me one Refined Oil of each element -Fire, Frost, Acid and Arcane- along with the gold, and I will teach you the recipe I keep for those who truly master the craft."
DescFinal=The four Refined oils, intact, and the gold counted down to the last coin. Few Alchemists make it this far. The Superior oil recipe is yours now: use it wisely, a good distillate is worth more than a whole weapon.
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=33
PosMap=294

[QUEST904]
Nombre=The Legendary Forging
Desc=Thirga strikes the anvil once, and the echo takes its time to fade. "You already know how to set an orb. Now I will teach you what I only teach once in a lifetime: the Legendary Elemental Forging, and the secret of the thorns that no common smith knows. I need 200 Iron Ingots, 100 Silver Ingots and 1,000,000 gold coins -the price of a life devoted to the hammer. Bring me all of that and both recipes are yours."
DescFinal=The ingots stacked, the gold counted. Thirga nods slowly, like someone handing over something she will not get back. "Now you forge like me. May the fire of your forge never fade, Worker."
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=40
PosMap=594

[QUEST905]
Nombre=The Perfect Arrow
Desc=The Cabinetmaker runs his hand along a shaft of elven wood, checking its straightness against the light. "A whole life carving arrows and only now have I made a truly perfect one. Bring me 100 Elven Arrows -to take apart and study their grain- and 500,000 gold coins to buy the fine tools I'm missing, and I will teach you to craft the Superior arrow: the one no archer in this world can match."
DescFinal=The hundred arrows disassembled on the table, the gold locked in the safe. The Cabinetmaker smiles for the first time. "There it is: the recipe for the perfect arrow. May it fly straight, Worker."
Repetible=0
RequiredLevel=40
PosMap=34

